// T26 & T27 (RFC §14): partitioned node records a local revocation unseen by the coordinator,
// while an unfenced new-host activation races the unexpired lease -> double-authority violation!
//! explore-domain: duration = 1, 3
Fact node Identified by N1, N2.
Fact active-lease Identified by node.
Fact local-revoked Identified by node.
Fact unfenced-restored Identified by node.

Act grant-lease Actor actor Related to node
  Holds when !active-lease(node)
  Valid when !active-lease(node)
  Creates active-lease(node) For 3.

// Disconnected local revocation on partitioned node N1 (unseen globally):
Event partitioned-local-revoke Related to node
  Creates local-revoked(node).

// Buggy coordinator activates N2 without waiting for N1's lease fence to expire:
Act unfenced-activate Actor actor Related to node
  Holds when !active-lease(node)
  Creates unfenced-restored(node).

// Single-authority fails if `unfenced-restored(N2)` coexists with unexpired `active-lease(N1)`:
Invariant single-authority-fenced
  When !(Exists node, node': active-lease(node) && unfenced-restored(node') && node != node').

+actor("Coord").
grant-lease("Coord", N1).
